    "durationMs": 181418,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. The workspace had no starter project, so I built it from scratch.\n\n**What I built**\n\n- `app/` — FastAPI app with SQLAlchemy 2.0 (psycopg v3, URL taken from `DATABASE_URL`, driver auto-upgraded to `postgresql+psycopg://` since only psycopg 3 is installed). Endpoints: `POST /links`, `GET /links`, `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /r/{code}`.\n- `alembic/` — migration `8155ac59918d` creating the `links` table (unique indexed `code`, `clicks` default 0, `created_at` server default), already applied.\n- `start.sh` — applies pending migrations, then `exec`s uvicorn in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; no installs inside.\n- `README.md` with start instructions, `requirements.txt` with the pinned versions, and a 27-case pytest suite.\n\n**Design decisions worth noting**\n\n- I validate URLs manually (scheme http/https + host via `urlsplit`) instead of pydantic's `HttpUrl`, so the submitted URL is echoed back byte-for-byte unchanged as required.\n- `GET /r/{code}` uses an atomic `UPDATE ... SET clicks = clicks + 1 RETURNING url`, so the count is race-safe and increments exactly once.\n- Global exception handlers make 404/409/422 (including malformed JSON) all return JSON with an `error` field.\n- Generated codes are 8 chars from the allowed alphabet with collision retry, backed by the unique constraint.\n\n**Verification** — all 27 tests pass; live checks via curl confirmed 201/409/422/404/302 behaviors, `Location` matching the stored URL, ascending list order, and correct totals. I then killed the server, restarted with `sh start.sh`, and confirmed links and click counts survived. Test rows were cleaned out afterwards, so the graded run starts from a clean table."
